WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.610
- On your new album,

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:03.480
there's a song called, "Smiling," and

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.430
I love it so much!

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.410
Because it's not,

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.527
I know a lot of people will say,

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:10.900
"Oh, that's for people in the limelight."

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.803
It's not. That's for
people in any vocation,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.320
any part of your life,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.137
you can be having that
moment where it's like,

00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:20.547
"I'm going through so much,

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:21.917
"but I guess I'll keep smiling

00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:23.597
"since that's what everyone's expecting,

00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:27.280
"and I'm supposed to be fine," you know?

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.090
- Especially as women too, right.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.600
I mean, we're sort of, archetypally,

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.050
it's almost like a demand to
be that hearth overseeing,

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.620
nurturing, which is normal
for us in our bodies,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.360
but we're also applying ourselves

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.070
in this whole yang world too.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.800
So, for me, it's all these different

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.050
archetypes that I love being.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.750
The teacher, the mom, the artist,

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.890
the activist, the outspoken,

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.400
you know, the channeler, all
these different archetypes,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.380
and just the hats, you know,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.910
I mean, I'm talking to you.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.410
You, of all people, know the
hats of mom, and then producer.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.020
So, just going through
all these different roles,

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.520
and because of the sensitivity,
and the empath qualities,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.910
I'm just so much more responsible

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.260
for making sure I can take breaks,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.960
even if it's hiding in a bathroom.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.300
I mean, you know, carrying
ear plugs with me,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.905
don't tell anybody. (laughs)

00:01:17.905 --> 00:01:18.738
- No, no, no.

00:01:18.738 --> 00:01:19.571
- I'm wearing them right now.

00:01:19.571 --> 00:01:20.528
No, just kidding.

00:01:20.528 --> 00:01:22.470
(both laughing)

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.740
I'm reading your lips.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.080
- I'm actually not listening to you.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.930
- Can't hear a word you're
saying, Kelly. (laughing)

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.550
- No, that's so true.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.500
Literally, I've had this conversation

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.333
with someone very close to me,

00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.427
and I'm like, "I'm not trying to be rude.

00:01:36.427 --> 00:01:38.127
"Like when I pull out the ear buds,

00:01:38.127 --> 00:01:39.497
"and like the music,

00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:42.217
"sometimes I'm not even playing anything.

00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:43.560
"I just want silence."

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.890
I just want a moment to where
I'm not being talked at,

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.810
or I don't feel like I'm having to engage.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.040
'Cause I feel like just
not our jobs, all jobs,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.671
I feel like we're a society

00:01:52.671 --> 00:01:54.660
that is constantly-
- It's a society of onness.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.920
Like the off,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.230
I mean, our nervous systems
were not meant to be

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:03.240
in cortisol mode 24/7, and
we're actually chronic stress

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.947
in the way that we're all experiencing

00:02:04.947 --> 00:02:06.134
is traumatic.
- Fight or flight, yeah.

00:02:06.134 --> 00:02:07.980
- It's traumatic.
- Yeah, it's constant,

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.230
I know, I know.

